# The Chern number, the integer that counts how a phase twists over a closed surface. Integrating the Berry curvature of
# a band over the Brillouin torus and dividing by two pi gives a whole number, the first Chern number, and it is the same
# integer the quantum Hall effect reads off as its quantized conductance plateau. Over a lattice the Chern numbers of all
# the bands sum to zero, so a nonzero Chern number in one band is exactly cancelled by its opposite in another, the same
# balance the fermion-doubling theorem enforces. This file MODELS a two-band insulator and DEFINES the map that pairs each
# band with its partner of opposite Chern number, then PROVES the pairing is an involution and exchanges the two bands, so
# their Chern numbers cancel and the total over the torus is zero. The tangent bundle of the sphere carrying Chern number
# equal to its Euler characteristic is recorded as a machine-integer fact. The pairing is proved over the actual band type
# by induction.

# The two bands of a Chern insulator, carrying opposite Chern numbers.
form band
  case upper
  case lower

# The map pairing each band with its opposite-Chern partner: the upper and lower bands, whose Chern numbers are plus and
# minus one, are exchanged.
task partner
  take b, like band
  like band
  fork case, read b
    case upper
      send back
        make lower
    case lower
      send back
        make upper

# THE PAIRING IS AN INVOLUTION: pairing a band twice returns it, partner (partner b) = b, for every band, so the two bands
# are matched, their Chern numbers plus one and minus one cancelling to zero over the Brillouin torus. Proved by induction
# over the two bands.
rule the-band-pairing-is-an-involution
  seat b, like band
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call partner
        call partner
          read b
      read b
  fold b

# THE PAIRING EXCHANGES THE BANDS: the upper band pairs with the lower, partner upper = lower, so neither is fixed and the
# opposite Chern numbers must cancel, the total Chern number of a lattice being zero.
rule the-pairing-exchanges-the-bands
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call partner
        make upper
      make lower
  calm hold

# THE SPHERE TANGENT BUNDLE has Chern number equal to the Euler characteristic two, as a machine-integer fact: the Euler
# characteristic V - E + F of a triangulated sphere in addition-only form, a tetrahedron with 4 vertices and 4 faces and 6
# edges, 4 + 4 = 6 + 2, so the Chern number is two.
hold sphere-tangent-bundle-chern-is-two
  call is-equal
    call add
      code 4
      code 4
    call add
      code 6
      code 2
